<section class="selected-work" aria-labelledby="selected-work-heading">
  <h2 id="selected-work-heading" class="section-label">
    02 / SELECTED WORK
  </h2>
  <article class="project" aria-labelledby="surtr-title">
    <header class="project-identity">
      <h3 id="surtr-title">Surtr Alert</h3>
      <p>Python notification plugin for WeeChat on Linux</p>
    </header>

    <div class="project-narrative">
      <p class="project-problem">
        Relevant IRC activity can be easy to miss when attention is elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        Surtr Alert adds local notifications for channel mentions, private messages and IRC notices,
        with optional alerts when configured friends join or leave.
      </p>
      <p>
        Python callbacks respond to WeeChat signal hooks, while settings stay in WeeChat’s native
        plugin configuration. No external web service is required.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="notification-path">
      <figcaption>
        <span class="section-label">FROM IRC ACTIVITY TO A LOCAL ALERT</span>
        <span class="path-caption">
          Conceptual inputs and outputs, not execution or fallback order.
        </span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="path-details">
        <div class="path-side">
          <h4>WeeChat events</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>channel mentions</li>
            <li>private messages</li>
            <li>IRC notices</li>
            <li>configured friend activity</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="path-boundary">
          <p>Python signal hooks</p>
          <p>Available controls: monitored-channel filters and ignored nicks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-side">
          <h4>Local notification</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>notify-send</li>
            <li>terminal</li>
            <li>Zenity</li>
            <li>local log</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="configuration-note">Settings stored in WeeChat.</p>
    </figure>

    <a
      class="repository-link"
      href="https://github.com/SrMetus/surtr-alert"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      View repository →
    </a>
  </article>
</section>

